.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OPENSSL-CRL2PKCS7 1ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openssl-crl2pkcs7
.Nd Create a PKCS#7 structure from a CRL and certificates
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm openssl
.Ar crl2pkcs7
.Oo
.Fl help ]
.Oo
.Fl inform
.Ar DER Ns | Ns Ar PEM ]
.Oo
.Fl outform
.Ar DER Ns | Ns Ar PEM ]
.Oo
.Fl in
.Em filename ]
.Oo
.Fl out
.Em filename ]
.Oo
.Fl certfile
.Em filename ]
.Oo
.Fl nocrl ]
.Oo
.Fl provider
.Em name ]
.Oo
.Fl provider-path
.Em path ]
.Oo
.Fl provparam
.Em [name:]key=value ]
.Oo
.Fl propquery
.Em propq ]
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This command takes an optional CRL and one or more certificates and
converts them into a PKCS#7 degenerate "certificates only" structure.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy -help
Print out a usage message.
.It Sy -inform Sy DER Ns | Ns Sy PEM
The input format of the CRL; the default is
.Sy PEM .
See
.Xr openssl-format-options 1
for details.
.It Sy -outform Sy DER Ns | Ns Sy PEM
The output format of the PKCS#7 object; the default is
.Sy PEM .
See
.Xr openssl-format-options 1
for details.
.It Sy -in Em filename
This specifies the input filename to read a CRL from or standard input
if this option is not specified.
.It Sy -out Em filename
Specifies the output filename to write the PKCS#7 structure to or
standard output by default.
.It Sy -certfile Em filename
Specifies a filename containing one or more certificates in
.Sy PEM
format.
All certificates in the file will be added to the PKCS#7 structure.
This option can be used more than once to read certificates from
multiple files.
.It Sy -nocrl
Normally a CRL is included in the output file.
With this option no CRL is included in the output file and a CRL is not
read from the input file.
.It Sy -provider Em name
.It Sy -provider-path Em path
.It Sy -provparam Em [name:]key=value
.It Sy -propquery Em propq
See
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr provider 7 ,
and
.Xr property 7 .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a PKCS#7 structure from a certificate and CRL:
.Bd -literal
 openssl crl2pkcs7 -in crl.pem -certfile cert.pem -out p7.pem
.Ed
.Pp
Creates a PKCS#7 structure in DER format with no CRL from several
different certificates:
.Bd -literal
 openssl crl2pkcs7 -nocrl -certfile newcert.pem
        -certfile demoCA/cacert.pem -outform DER -out p7.der
.Ed
.Sh NOTES
The output file is a PKCS#7 signed data structure containing no signers
and just certificates and an optional CRL.
.Pp
This command can be used to send certificates and CAs to Netscape as
part of the certificate enrollment process.
This involves sending the DER encoded output as MIME type
application/x-x509-user-cert.
.Pp
The
.Sy PEM
encoded form with the header and footer lines removed can be used to
install user certificates and CAs in MSIE using the Xenroll control.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr openssl-pkcs7 1
